# PostgreSQL Standards

Use:

- snake_case
- UUID PKs
- timestamptz
- explicit FK names
- explicit constraint names
- named indexes

Normalize whenever practical.

Enums belong ONLY to 001.

Avoid:

- duplicated data
- duplicated constraints
- unnecessary JSONB

Every FK must have intentional ON DELETE behaviour.

Every NOT NULL column must be justified.

Generated columns must be deterministic.

Indexes must support:

- FK lookups
- tenant filtering
- common search paths

Never sacrifice integrity for convenience.